package server

const mcpAnalyticsPolicy = "Time Series & Signal Analysis uses optional schema-version-1 diagram.analytics, never a separate database or Process Simulator capacity model. GET /analytics/capabilities discovers implemented methods, units, warm-up, defaults and independent computation/transport limits. GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/analytics returns compact semantic configuration by default; full=true returns the complete bounded extension. Raw series queries and worker results are paginated. Saved dataset, series, chart, indicator, measurement, rule, backtest and scenario CRUD uses current baseVersion; definitions never depend on canvas pixels. Exact POST analytics measure, indicator, evaluate, validate, project, waterfall, compare, export, query, import/inspect, import/preview and jobs are unsaved read-only operations. Job archive and import/commit require write access. XLSX is padded base64; CSV/JSON source uses text. Import commit requires an explicitly reviewed confirmed:true and create/replace/update mode. Missing observations remain missing, rate numerators/denominators must be compatible, and scenarios never overwrite observed history. Local seeded/numeric analysis uses the same worker engine as UI and headless requests. Background jobs retain the original unlocked vault session and grant, expose progress/cancel and are erased on revocation, lock or reload. Clients must check direct bridge health for analytics-v1 and update an old local binary explicitly; a website refresh does not update that binary. No analysis unlocks or extends idle sessions, sends imported business data to AI, invents predictive confidence or runs alarms after the browser closes."

const mcpAnalyticsGuide = `

## Time Series & Signal Analysis

This template is an optional diagram.analytics extension with schemaVersion:1 on an existing diagram type. Discover GET /analytics/capabilities and GET /diagrams?analytics=true first; compact discovery omits observations and archives. do not infer analytics from canvas positions. Bridge 0.11.0 direct GET /api/v1/health advertises analytics-v1. An old bridge must be rebuilt/replaced explicitly: updating the website does not update its local binary.

Use visual_nerve_api_docs with document:"guide" before workspace commands, then document:"endpoint" with path:"/diagrams/{diagramId}/analytics/import/commit" and method:"POST" for the exact import contract and all referenced schemas. visual_nerve_request uses paths without /api/v1; the existing tools are unchanged. Keep https://app.visualnerve.com/ human-unlocked with the exact --allowed-origin https://app.visualnerve.com and a current grant. The public help/API website is https://www.visualnerve.com/; there is no production editor at app-origin /app/.

GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/analytics returns {diagramId,baseVersion,analytics}; compact datasets contain observationCount rather than raw observations and result summaries omit retained input. full=true requests the complete extension, subject to the separate 8 MiB analytics response budget. PUT the complete extension using {baseVersion,value}. Mutation acknowledgements use the same compact {diagramId,baseVersion,analytics} shape, with the new saved version. The UI reloads that authoritative local graph. Collections datasets, series, charts, indicators, measurements, rules, backtests and scenarios support GET/POST and entity GET/PATCH/DELETE: saved writes use {baseVersion,value}, and DELETE uses ?baseVersion=N. Read the exact schema and current canonical semantic identities before changing configuration.

For own data, POST .../analytics/import/inspect with {source,seriesColumn?} to discover columns/sheets and optional long-series names. Then POST .../analytics/import/preview with {datasetId,source,mapping}; source is {kind:"csv"|"json",name,text} or {kind:"xlsx",name,data:base64,sheet?}. Decimal/percent/date/timezone conventions, wide/long columns, duplicate policy and missing/invalid-row policies are explicit. Review issues and row counts, then use POST .../analytics/import/commit with {baseVersion,input,mode:"create"|"replace"|"update",confirmed:true}. There is no partial model save on rejected preview. The browser's file limit does not increase the 32 MiB HTTP/WebSocket transport budget.

POST .../analytics/query?offset=0&limit=100 with {seriesId,from?,to?,resolution?,dimensions?,cutoff?,ohlc?} returns data pages. Explicit aggregation follows snapshot/flow/rate semantics; it never computes temporal cohort churn from pooled segment rates. An incompatible unit or absent risk denominator is a structured error.

Stored/API timestamps use canonical UTC millisecond ISO, for example 2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z. Imports normalize selected date/time conventions. Pure previews permit Read only: POST .../analytics/measure with {id} or {measurement}; /indicator with {id} or {indicator}; /evaluate with {ruleIds?,from?,to?}; /validate with {id} or {config}; /project with {id} or {scenario}; /waterfall with {id,time} or {chart,time}. /compare with {scenarioIds:[...]} requires identical start, resolution, horizon and currency. /export?offset=0&limit=100 returns json/csv pages for observations, measurements, signals or scenarios. POST /export without paging also accepts {scope:"chart"|"indicator"|"scenario"|"measurement",id,format:"svg",options:{width?,height?,appearance:"light"|"dark",from?,to?,dimensions?,maxPoints?,time?}} for a bounded DOM-free vector chart. Measurement SVG supports saved regression definitions only and plots actual shared-engine fitted values; other measurement kinds retain JSON/CSV export. Waterfall requires options.time; SVG preserves separate unit panels and reports rendered/source counts and sampling warnings. Calculations are the same as the UI, with observed/derived/scenario values separate. Signals record observation and first possible detection timestamps, onset/active/resolved episodes and causal evidence. Signal handling fields do not modify calculated evidence. A backtest without an explicit outcome returns history rather than fabricated precision/recall. Growth & Churn projections state assumptions and are not guaranteed forecasts.

POST .../analytics/jobs with {kind:"measurement"|"indicator"|"signals"|"backtest"|"scenario"|"import"|"inspect-import"|"query"|"waterfall",input} starts a transient bounded worker calculation. GET /jobs/{jobId} reads 0..100 progress; GET /jobs/{jobId}/result?offset=0&limit=100 returns semantic summary and item pages with nextOffset. DELETE /jobs/{jobId} cancels/erases it and permits Read only. POST /jobs/{jobId}/archive with {baseVersion} is a write; import archives additionally require mode and confirmed:true. Inspection/query/waterfall view jobs cannot be archived. At most two API jobs run, four terminal jobs and 32 MiB of original input/results are retained for 15 minutes; calculation deadline is 120 seconds. Existing results preserve immutable original input and data/rule/engine versions. Lock, grant changes, reload and TTL remove temporary jobs; they cannot be recovered by a new grant. Saved archives persist through encrypted storage/backup and can be explicitly deleted with their original input. GET /results returns compact metadata, /results/{entityId}/content pages numerical output, and /results/{entityId}/input returns original configuration; add ?datasetId=ID&offset=0&limit=100 for retained original observations after refresh. Regression item pages pair fitted value and residual. Signals distinguish observed value/unit from deviationMagnitude/deviationUnit/thresholdUnit and report total/omitted bounded publication counts.

Write recovery uses the existing POST /operations reservation and operationId. After timeout read the same receipt, never repeat a write under a new identity blindly. Recovery is bounded to the original browser/grant and does not guarantee exactly-once behavior across reloads. No new tool, server database, automatic process mutation or AI connection is introduced. Live or headless analysis still requires an available unlocked browser; no server-side alarm is promised when it closes.
`
